vely, the user could use `UserHoldout(validation_size=1, test_size=1)` (1 interaction per user for validation, 1 for test) but this again changes proportions.\n\nThe most faithful fix to the original experimental design would be to use `UserHoldout(validation_size=1, test_size=1)` which holds out 1 interaction per user for validation and 1 for test (approximately an 80/10/10 split depending on user history length), and then simply not evaluate on the validation set.\n\n                    NEXT STEPS FOR DEBUGGING:\n                    - Review the error message above carefully\n                    - Check for missing imports or incorrect package names\n                    - Verify variable names and function calls\n                    - Ensure all required data files are accessible\n                    - Consider simplifying the code to isolate the issue\n\n                    This implementation failed execution. Focus on resolving the error before optimizing.\n\nBelow is a list of requirements that are not yet met and some feedback for each:\n- Requirement: 5. [Data Splitting] The experiment MUST use UserHoldout(validation_size=0.0, test_size=0.2) for user-based 80/20 train/test split.\n- Feedback: The implementation uses `UserHoldout(validation_size=0.0, test_size=0.2)` as required, but it crashes because `UserHoldout._process` computes `test_size=self._valid_size/(1-self._test_size) = 0.0/0.8 = 0.0` for the second `train_test_split` call, and sklearn does not accept `test_size=0.0` as a float. To fix this, either set `validation_size` to a small positive value like 0.05 and adjust test_size accordingly for true 80/20 split, or modify the pipeline to skip the validation split step when validation_size is 0.\n\n- Requirement: 7. [Algorithms] Three algorithms MUST be tested: LensKit.ImplicitMFScorer (ALS), LensKit.ItemKNNScorer, and LensKit.PopScorer, all configured with feedback='implicit' and default hyperparameters.\n- Feedback: The algorithms are correctly specified (LensKit.PopScorer, LensKit.ItemKNNScorer, LensKit.ImplicitMFScorer with feedback='implicit') but are never actually tested because the code crashes during preprocessing due to UserHoldout(validation_size=0.0) — UserHoldout always creates a 3-way split and train_test_split cannot accept test_size=0.0. The algorithms must actually be executed (trained and evaluated) to fulfill 'MUST be tested'. Fix the split to use a positive validation_size or use a different splitting approach.\n\n- Requirement: 9. [Full Factorial Design] The experiment MUST execute a full factorial design: all 3 algorithms x all 3 datasets x all 5 seeds = 45 runs.\n- Feedback: The experiment crashes on the first seed and first dataset due to passing validation_size=0.0 to UserHoldout, which is invalid (train_test_split requires test_size > 0). This prevents any of the 45 runs from executing, so the full factorial design is not fulfilled. To fix, use a small positive validation_size (e.g., 0.1) or use a different split approach that doesn't require validation.\n\n- Requirement: 10. [Results & Statistical Analysis] Results MUST be reported in tabular form per (dataset, algorithm, seed) showing all metrics. The implementation MUST compute and report mean and standard deviation across the 5 seeds for each algorithm-dataset combination to quantify the impact of random seed variation on accuracy.\n- Feedback: The program crashes on the first seed/dataset due to UserHoldout(validation_size=0.0, test_size=0.2) passing 0.0 as validation_size, which causes sklearn's train_test_split to receive test_size=0.0 internally and raise an InvalidParameterError. No results are produced, so the requirement is not fulfilled. Fix: use a small positive validation size (e.g., UserHoldout(validation_size=0.1, test_size=0.2)) or use a split that doesn't require a validation set.\n", is_satisfactory=False)
